  "english": "8. Sunday, Tone 3 [B2 / BG]. Ninth Sunday [after Pentecost / after the Cross]. Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 3 [b2]: \"In the Grave\" (I gerezman) and \"They Came to the Grave\" (Yekin i gerezman). Tone of glad tidings.\n15. Sunday, Tone 4 [A2 / AK]. Tenth Sunday. Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 4 [ak]: \"Wonderful\" (Skancheli), to the end. Eve of the Fast of Fifty Days [Advent].\n16. Monday, Tone 3 [B2 / BG]. Fast of Fifty Days [Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 8 [d2 / DZ]: \"God of our fathers, Who art...\" (Z-Hartsyn merots astuadz vor ap).\n21. Saturday, Tone 8 [D2 / DK]. Feast of the Presentation of the Holy Mother of God of Three Years.\n22. Sunday, Tone 1 [A1 / ADZ]. First Sunday [of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [g1 / GDZ]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord\". Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 1 [adz]: \"With the Women\" (Ynd kanaysn) and \"Who Ineffable\" (Vor ancharr).\n23. Monday, Tone 2 [A2 / AK]. Feast of Julian and Basil. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 3 [b2]: \"Without Malice\" (Anokhakal).\n25. Wednesday, Tone 4 [B2 / BK]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 7 [d1 / DDZ]: \"Truly\" (Tshmartapes).\n29. Sunday, Tone 8 [D2 / DK]. Second Sunday [of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 4 [ak]: \"Beginningless Word\" (Anskizbn band). Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 8 [dk]: \"Thine Angel, O Lord\" (Hreshtak ko ter).\n\nDecember\n5. Saturday, Tone 6 [G2 / GK]. Feast of Nicholas and Gregory the Wonderworker, Patriarchs; and of the other Nicholas, Patriarch, and Myron, Bishop. At Morning Service [Mankunk] melody: \"They Were Amazed\" (Hiatsan). Midday Liturgy [Chashu] Patristic Hymn Tone 3 [b2]: \"Who with Light\" (Vor lusov).\n6. Sunday, Tone 7 [D1 / DDZ]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 3 [b2]: \"Incorruptible\" (Anapakan). Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 5 [g1 / GDZ]: \"Who Art Above\" (Vor i verd es). Eve of the Fast of Saint James.\n9. Wednesday, Tone 2 [A2 / AK]. Fast. Feast of the Conception of the Holy Virgin by Anna.\n13. Sunday, Tone 6 [G2 / GK]. Fourth Sunday [of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 4 [bk]: \"Beginningless God\" (Anskizbn astuadz). Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 6 [gk]: \"Taking [flesh] from us\" (Arrheal yev mer).\n20. Sunday, Tone 5 [G1 / GDZ]. Fifth Sunday [of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 5 [g1 / GDZ]: \"O Glorified Son\" (Z-Paravoreal vordi). Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 5 [g1 / GDZ]: \"Oil-bearing [Women] and Holy\" (Yughaber yev surb), to the end.\n21. Monday, Tone 6 [G2 / GK]. Feast of Abraham and Khoren, [and of] Cosmas and Damian. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 7 [d1 / DDZ]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord of Hosts\".\n22. Tuesday, Tone 7 [D1 / DDZ]. Feast of Adeodatus [Astvadsatur] the Witness. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 8 [dk]: \"To Thee, O God\" (Arr kez astuadz).\n24. Thursday, Tone 1 [A1 / ADZ]. Feast of David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n27. Sunday, Tone 4 [B2 / BK]. Sixth Sunday [of Advent]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 6 [gk]: \"Pre-eternal\" (Nakhahavitean). Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 4 [bk]: \"They Antedated\" (Kankhetsin), to the end.\n29. Tuesday, Tone 6 [G2 / GK]. Feast of the Sons of Thunder: James and John. Eve of the Fast of the Nativity.\n30. Wednesday, Tone 7 [D1 / DDZ]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] of the Fast, Tone 8 [dk]: \"Blessed art Thou, Lord God of our fathers\".\n\nJanuary\n3. Sunday, Tone 3 [B2 / BG]. Seventh Sunday [of Advent], of the Fast. Evening [Hambartsi] Hymn Tone 3 [b2]: \"Today They Rejoiced\" (Aysor zuarchatsan), to the end.\n5. Tuesday, Tone 5 [G1 / GDZ]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ [Theophany].\n\nROMAN SEVEN-DAY CYCLE 3\n16. Thursday. Feast of Peter the Patriarch, Blaise, and others.\n18. Monday. Feast of Anthony, and Triphon, Barsamas, and Onuphrius the Hermits.\n19. Sunday. First Sunday [after Nativity/Epiphany]. Canticle of the Fathers [Harts] Tone 7 [d1 / DDZ]: \"The Dawn of the Only-Begotten\" (Dagunm miadzni).\n\nJanuary\n6. MONDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Theophany of Christ. The period of abstinence-free days [post-feast] is twenty-eight days.\n14. Tuesday. Feast of John the Forerunner.",
